From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timon Stipkovits <timon2201@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] mm: ignore the watermark boost in the remaining "would
 the allocation succeed" checks

Patch 0002 made zone_watermark_fast() ignore zone->watermark_boost when
an allocation checks the min watermark, and allow_direct_reclaim() use
the unboosted min watermark for the pfmemalloc reserve. Three checks
that ask whether that same allocation would succeed still use
min_wmark_pages(), which includes the boost:

- should_reclaim_retry() decides whether the allocator keeps looping
  through direct reclaim by asking whether free plus reclaimable pages
  would meet the min watermark. With the boost the answer can be "no"
  while the allocation itself, checked without the boost, would
  succeed after reclaim; the allocator then stops retrying early and
  heads for compaction retries or the OOM path.

- should_continue_reclaim() stops reclaim/compaction (high-order
  reclaim, direct and kswapd) once the allocation can already succeed.
  With the boost that point is reached only min + boost pages later,
  so a reclaimer keeps reclaiming after its allocation would already
  have gone through.

- compaction_ready() lets shrink_zones() skip reclaim of a zone when
  the costly-order allocation can already succeed. With the boost it
  says "reclaim first" in the same situation.

While a boost is active (it is raised by every pageblock steal and
worked off by kswapd), the last two make high-order direct reclaim run
longer than the allocation needs, in the allocating task. Use the
unboosted min watermark, zone->_watermark[WMARK_MIN], for these three
checks, the same value zone_watermark_fast() now uses.

should_continue_reclaim() also passes the watermark to
compaction_suitable(). That one keeps the boosted value:
compaction_suit_allocation_order() runs the same check with the boosted
watermark before direct compaction starts, and stopping reclaim at a
lower line would only make compaction return COMPACT_SKIPPED and send
the allocator back into reclaim.

Checks against the low and high watermarks, where the boost is meant to
apply, and the order-0 margins compaction keeps for its migration
targets are unchanged.

Depends on "mm/page_alloc: don't apply watermark boost to the min
watermark".

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 mm/page_alloc.c |  9 ++++++++-
 mm/vmscan.c     | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/page_alloc.c b/mm/page_alloc.c
index 8d880204b..43e8ad909 100644
--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -4678,7 +4678,14 @@ should_reclaim_retry(gfp_t gfp_mask, unsigned order,
 				ac->highest_zoneidx, ac->nodemask) {
 		unsigned long available;
 		unsigned long reclaimable;
-		unsigned long min_wmark = min_wmark_pages(zone);
+		/*
+		 * The allocation attempts above check the min watermark
+		 * without the boost (see zone_watermark_fast()), so ask the
+		 * same question here: with the boost, a zone whose free plus
+		 * reclaimable pages would satisfy the allocation could be
+		 * given up on while the boost is still being worked off.
+		 */
+		unsigned long min_wmark = zone->_watermark[WMARK_MIN];
 		bool wmark;
 
 		if (cpusets_enabled() &&
diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
index ee28f7747..d3a7ef016 100644
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -6258,8 +6258,15 @@ static inline bool should_continue_reclaim(struct pglist_data *pgdat,
 	for_each_managed_zone_pgdat(zone, pgdat, z, sc->reclaim_idx) {
 		unsigned long watermark = min_wmark_pages(zone);
 
-		/* Allocation can already succeed, nothing to do */
-		if (zone_watermark_ok(zone, sc->order, watermark,
+		/*
+		 * Allocation can already succeed, nothing to do. The
+		 * allocator ignores the boost at the min watermark (see
+		 * zone_watermark_fast()), so do the same here. The
+		 * compaction_suitable() check below keeps the boosted value
+		 * to match the check compaction itself makes before it runs.
+		 */
+		if (zone_watermark_ok(zone, sc->order,
+				      zone->_watermark[WMARK_MIN],
 				      sc->reclaim_idx, 0))
 			return false;
 
@@ -6484,8 +6491,11 @@ static inline bool compaction_ready(struct zone *zone, struct scan_control *sc)
 	if (!gfp_compaction_allowed(sc->gfp_mask))
 		return false;
 
-	/* Allocation can already succeed, nothing to do */
-	if (zone_watermark_ok(zone, sc->order, min_wmark_pages(zone),
+	/*
+	 * Allocation can already succeed, nothing to do. Like the allocator
+	 * (see zone_watermark_fast()), ignore the boost at the min watermark.
+	 */
+	if (zone_watermark_ok(zone, sc->order, zone->_watermark[WMARK_MIN],
 			      sc->reclaim_idx, 0))
 		return true;
 
